  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile models with scvi_n200 perform best, with avgpool and transformer aggregation giving similar high accuracy (~0.65) and F1. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the scgpt RNA representation can match or exceed scvi_n200 under the same favorable multiprofile/avgpool setting. config_008 tests this by changing only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt, isolating the representation effect. This is the best next experiment because it is both potentially high-performing and informative, while avoiding confounding changes to image encoder, fusion, or aggregation before deciding whether multimodal configurations are worthwhile."
